          },
          {
            "tag": "p",
            "text": "CodeQL 2.23.9 has been released January 20, 2026 Strengthen your supply chain with code-to-cloud traceability and SLSA Build Level 3 security January 20, 2026 Enterprise-scoped budgets that exclude cost center usage in public preview January 19, 2026 GitHub Copilot now supports OpenCode January 16, 2026 View all changes Engineering More engineering articles Post-quantum security for SSH access on GitHub GitHub is introducing post-quantum secure key exchange methods for SSH access to better protect Git data in transit."
          },
          {
            "tag": "h3",
            "text": "How GitHub engineers tackle platform problems"
          },
          {
            "tag": "p",
            "text": "Our best practices for quickly identifying, resolving, and preventing issues at scale."
          },
          {
            "tag": "h3",
            "text": "GitHub Issues search now supports nested queries and boolean operators: Here&#8217;s how we (re)built it"
          },
          {
            "tag": "p",
            "text": "Plus, considerations in updating one of GitHub&#8217;s oldest and most heavily used features."
          },
          {
            "tag": "h3",
            "text": "Design system annotations, part 2: Advanced methods of annotating components"
          },
          {
            "tag": "p",
            "text": "How to build custom annotations for your design system components or use Figma’s Code Connect to help capture important accessibility details before development."
          },
          {
            "tag": "h3",
            "text": "Design system annotations, part 1: How accessibility gets left out of components"
          },
          {
            "tag": "p",
            "text": "The Accessibility Design team created a set of annotations to bridge the gaps that design systems alone can’t fix and proactively addresses accessibility issues within Primer components."
          },
          {
            "tag": "h2",
            "text": "Spotlight"
          },
          {
            "tag": "p",
            "text": "Octoverse 2025: AI, India, and the new #1 programming language Dive into the key findings from Octoverse 2025! This year saw record-breaking growth with over 180 million developers now on GitHub. We explore three big shifts: generative AI becoming ordinary engineering, TypeScript&#8217;s rise to the #1 language, and how AI is influencing developer choices. See how the developer map is redrawing itself faster than ever."
          },
          {
            "tag": "p",
            "text": "The untold story of Log4j and Log4Shell In late 2021, the Log4Shell vulnerability sent shockwaves through the global tech community. Hear the untold, inside story from Christian Grobmeier, a maintainer of the Log4j project."
          },
          {
            "tag": "p",
            "text": "Two decades of Git: A conversation with creator Linus Torvalds Twenty years ago, Linus Torvalds created the basis for Git in just 10 days, forever changing how developers collaborate on code. In this interview, Linus Torvalds discusses Git&#8217;s unexpected journey."
